# The Dockerfile copies the whole build context into nginx's web root, so
# anything left here is fetchable from the public site. nginx.conf only denies
# dotfiles, so this file is the only thing keeping the rest out.
#
# Before this list grew, https://marisstella.dev/nginx.conf served the server
# configuration and the CSP, and /package.json served the toolchain.
#
# This list is no longer the claim. `tests/markup-contract.test.mjs` resolves
# these patterns against the directory as it actually is, and requires what
# survives to equal the --from-file set in platform/ci/deploy-homepage.sh — so
# a new file here is a failing test, not a silent publication. It caught this
# list carrying `test` while the directory on disk was `tests`: every test
# source and the DOM fixture were being served from the public web root.
.git
.github
.dockerignore
node_modules
coverage
*.log
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
Dockerfile
Dockerfile*
nginx.conf
package.json
package-lock.json
tests
output
e2e
e2e-report
e2e-results
playwright.config.ts
*.png
